From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
Date: Fri, 21 Jun 2024 17:44:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: nvme-tcp: Do not terminate commands when in
 RESETTING
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the error recovery started it will terminate all commands
anyway, so we should just return BLK_EH_RESET_TIMER for a
command timeout.

Signed-off-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
Acked-by: Daniel Wagner <dwagner@suse.de>
Signed-off-by: Alexander Mikhalitsyn <aleksandr.mikhalitsyn@canonical.com>
Tested-by: Julian Pelizäus <julian.pelizaeus@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Paolo Pisati <paolo.pisati@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00091
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@f042210c3ae176539280b04b71da817cd8a7f06c
---
 drivers/nvme/host/tcp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/tcp.c b/drivers/nvme/host/tcp.c
index ce28c9b03817..5dc64c0f1a07 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/tcp.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/tcp.c
@@ -2762,6 +2762,14 @@ static enum blk_eh_timer_return nvme_tcp_timeout(struct request *rq)
 		 rq->tag, nvme_cid(rq), pdu->hdr.type, cmd->common.opcode,
 		 nvme_fabrics_opcode_str(qid, cmd), qid);
 
+	/*
+	 * If the error recovery is started all commands will be
+	 * aborted anyway, and nothing is to be done here.
+	 */
+	if (nvme_ctrl_state(ctrl) == NVME_CTRL_RESETTING &&
+	    work_pending(&to_tcp_ctrl(ctrl)->err_work))
+		return BLK_EH_RESET_TIMER;
+
 	if (nvme_ctrl_state(ctrl) != NVME_CTRL_LIVE) {
 		/*
 		 * If we are resetting, connecting or deleting we should
